WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.540
[Intro music plays]

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:13.610
Host: Welcome to our podcast, where we dive
deep into the world of psychology and explore

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:19.220
the ways in which our minds can influence
our experiences.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:26.060
Today, we're going to talk about a phenomenon
that affects many people, regardless of their

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.859
success or achievements: imposter syndrome.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:30.619
[Transition music plays]

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:35.660
Host: Imposter syndrome is the experience
of feeling like a fraud or impostor, despite

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.010
evidence of your competence or accomplishments.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.960
It's a pervasive and often debilitating feeling
that can affect anyone, from high-achieving

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:49.480
professionals to students and artists.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:56.070
To better understand imposter syndrome, let's
take a closer look at what it is and how it

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.070
can affect us.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.070
Joining us today is Dr. Jane, a psychologist
and expert on imposter syndrome.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.070
Dr. Jane, thank you for joining us today.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:07.380
Can you start by telling us a little bit more
about what imposter syndrome is, and why it's

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.150
so common?

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:16.439
Dr. Jane: Sure.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:21.590
Imposter syndrome is a psychological phenomenon
where individuals doubt their own abilities

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:27.869
and accomplishments, and have a persistent
fear of being exposed as a fraud or impostor.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:34.810
It's common because it can affect anyone,
regardless of their background, success, or

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:40.240
achievements.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.049
In fact, research suggests that up to 70%
of people experience imposter syndrome at

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:47.890
some point in their lives.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:57.640
Host: That's a staggering number.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:14.640
So, what are some common signs and symptoms
of imposter syndrome?

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:30.410
Dr. Jane: Some common signs of imposter syndrome
include feeling like a fraud, doubting your

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:35.560
own abilities and accomplishments, constantly
seeking validation and reassurance from others,

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:59.450
and downplaying your own achievements.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:06.170
Individuals with imposter syndrome may also
experience anxiety, self-doubt, and fear of

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.260
failure.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:16.450
Host: And what are some of the underlying
factors that contribute to imposter syndrome?

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:24.530
Dr. Jane: There are several factors that can
contribute to imposter syndrome, including

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:32.670
perfectionism, social comparison, and a lack
of self-confidence.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.879
Perfectionists often set high standards for
themselves and feel like they can never live

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:43.299
up to them, which can contribute to feelings
of inadequacy and self-doubt.

00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:48.140
Social comparison, or comparing oneself to
others, can also contribute to imposter syndrome,

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:56.950
as individuals may feel like they don't measure
up to others who they perceive as more successful

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.939
or accomplished.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:07.400
Finally, a lack of self-confidence can make
it difficult to internalize one's own achievements

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.349
and accomplishments, which can contribute
to feelings of being a fraud or impostor.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:15.270
Host: That's really interesting.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:22.229
So, how can we overcome imposter syndrome
and start to feel more confident in our abilities?

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:29.290
Dr. Jane: There are several strategies that
can be helpful in overcoming imposter syndrome.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:41.660
One strategy is to practice self-compassion
and be kind to ourselves, rather than beating

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.650
ourselves up for perceived failures or shortcomings.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:52.509
It's also important to recognize and internalize
our own achievements and accomplishments,

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:57.800
rather than downplaying them or attributing
them to luck or other external factors.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.800
Seeking support from others, whether it's
through therapy, coaching, or talking to friends

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.600
and family, can also be helpful in overcoming
imposter syndrome.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.000
Host: Those are great tips.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.190
So, let's switch gears a little bit and talk
about imposter syndrome in the workplace.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:12.170
How can imposter syndrome affect our careers,
and what can we do to overcome it in a professional

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.170
setting?

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:17.710
Dr. Jane: Imposter syndrome can have a significant
impact on our careers, as it can lead us to

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.550
doubt our abilities and hold ourselves back
from pursuing new opportunities or taking

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.550
on new challenges.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.640
In the workplace, it can also contribute to
feelings of burnout and stress, as individuals

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:30.800
may feel like they need to constantly prove
themselves or work harder than others to compensate

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.840
for their perceived inadequacies.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.840
Here are some interesting facts about imposter
syndrome:

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:40.920
It affects people from all walks of life:
Imposter syndrome is not limited to any particular

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.289
profession or demographic.

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:46.660
It can affect anyone, regardless of their
age, gender, or background.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:57.410
It's more common than you think: Studies have
shown that up to 70% of people experience

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:02.400
imposter syndrome at some point in their lives.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:08.400
It's not a mental disorder: While imposter
syndrome can be distressing, it's not considered

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.400
a mental disorder.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.539
Rather, it's a common experience that many
people go through.

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:17.910
It can be caused by a variety of factors:
Imposter syndrome can be caused by a number

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.210
of factors, including perfectionism, social
comparison, and a lack of self-confidence.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.190
It can lead to burnout: People with imposter
syndrome may feel like they need to constantly

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:28.569
prove themselves or work harder than others,
which can lead to burnout and other negative

00:06:28.569 --> 00:06:29.569
outcomes.

00:06:29.569 --> 00:06:33.789
It can affect relationships: People with imposter
syndrome may struggle to accept compliments

00:06:33.789 --> 00:06:38.139
or may push others away, which can have a
negative impact on their relationships.

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:43.289
It's not always a bad thing: While imposter
syndrome can be distressing, it can also be

00:06:43.289 --> 00:06:46.590
a sign that you're pushing yourself out of
your comfort zone and taking on new challenges.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.041
It's important to recognize the positive aspects
of imposter syndrome and use it as motivation

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.039
to grow and develop.

00:06:51.039 --> 00:06:52.560
Imposter Syndrome personalities
Imposter syndrome can affect individuals from

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.949
all personality types and traits.

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:57.900
However, some personality traits may be more
prone to experiencing imposter syndrome than

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:58.900
others.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.330
Here are a few examples:

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:05.180
Perfectionists: People who are perfectionists
often set extremely high standards for themselves

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.629
and may struggle with feeling like they haven't
met those expectations.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:19.820
This can lead to imposter syndrome, as they
feel like they're not good enough or haven't

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.699
done enough.

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:39.599
Overachievers: Individuals who are overachievers
may experience imposter syndrome because they

00:07:39.599 --> 00:07:45.479
feel like they're not living up to their potential
or that their accomplishments aren't truly

00:07:45.479 --> 00:07:46.479
deserved.

00:07:46.479 --> 00:07:50.790
This can lead to a cycle of constantly pushing
themselves to achieve more.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:08:02.490
Introverts: Introverts may be more likely
to experience imposter syndrome because they

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:16.080
tend to be more introspective and may be more
likely to focus on their own shortcomings

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.080
or flaws.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.590
People pleasers: Individuals who are people
pleasers may struggle with imposter syndrome

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:27.530
because they worry about letting others down
or not living up to expectations.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:46.040
They may also feel like they're not being
true to themselves, which can lead to feelings

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.320
of self-doubt.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:09:00.080
Highly creative individuals: People who work
in creative fields may experience imposter

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:15.800
syndrome because they often have to put themselves
and their work out there for others to judge.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:29.850
They may worry that their work isn't good
enough or that they're not as talented as

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.089
others in their field.

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:45.790
It's important to note that while certain
personality traits may make someone more susceptible

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:56.440
to imposter syndrome, anyone can experience
it regardless of their personality type.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:10:07.041
There have been many famous people who have
openly talked about their struggles with imposter

00:10:07.041 --> 00:10:08.510
syndrome.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.660
Here are a few examples:

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:21.250
Maya Angelou: The late poet, author, and civil
rights activist Maya Angelou once said, "I

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:30.310
have written 11 books, but each time I think,
'uh oh, they're going to find out now.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:36.350
I've run a game on everybody, and they're
going to find me out.'"

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:42.510
Tom Hanks: The Oscar-winning actor Tom Hanks
has spoken publicly about his experience with

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:51.709
imposter syndrome, saying, "No matter what
we've done, there comes a point where you

00:10:51.709 --> 00:10:54.600
think, 'How did I get here?

00:10:54.600 --> 00:11:20.930
When are they going to discover that I am,
in fact, a fraud and take everything away

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:28.779
from me?'"

00:11:28.779 --> 00:12:58.320
Emma Watson: The actress and activist Emma
Watson has also 

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:19.760
talked about her struggles with imposter syndrome,
saying, "It's almost like the better I do,

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:36.529
the more my feeling of inadequacy actually
increases."

00:13:36.529 --> 00:13:50.910
Michelle Obama: The former First Lady Michelle
Obama has revealed in her memoir "Becoming"

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:55.250
that she has experienced imposter syndrome
throughout her life, saying, "I still have

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:59.720
a little bit of impostor syndrome, it never
goes away, that you're actually listening

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:04.019
to me...It doesn't go away, that feeling that
you shouldn't take me that seriously."

00:14:04.019 --> 00:14:11.800
Albert Einstein: The famous physicist Albert
Einstein once wrote in a letter, "The exaggerated

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:16.509
esteem in which my lifework is held makes
me very ill at ease.

00:14:16.509 --> 00:14:29.730
I feel compelled to think of myself as an
involuntary swindler."

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:39.550
These examples show that imposter syndrome
can affect anyone, regardless of their level

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:40.779
of success or accomplishments.

00:14:40.779 --> 00:14:44.120
It's important to recognize that imposter
syndrome is a common experience and seek support

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.100
if needed.

